From 5ed54f129a6f84febbd843c1a150bcd0f7acbd48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:28:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09266/11362] Pin the sampler seed and add an A/A control: the
 pipeline's noise floor is ~40%

Operator asked why the design needs 3 trials. Tracing it found something worse
than variance-averaging, and documented in the proposer's own docstring.

THE SOURCE OF NONDETERMINISM. Every generation goes out at
`temperature = 0.2 + 0.1*attempt` with NO seed field. llama-server reads an absent
seed as -1 = "pick a fresh random one". The harness `seed` argument seeds
random/numpy in the driver and never reaches the server's sampler. From
LocalGGUFProposer.sampling_seed, measured not assumed:

    "2 of 5 cells diverge under IDENTICAL CODE -- a 40% nondeterminism rate.
     That floor is at least as large as any treatment effect yet measured on this
     path, so an A/B here is uninterpretable without an A/A control no matter how
     many cells it runs."

So 3 trials was never variance-averaging over a well-behaved process. It is
partial mitigation for an uncontrolled floor, and the code says averaging does not
rescue it. We were 2 cells into a 51-hour run whose own harness documents it as
unreadable in that configuration.

TWO FIXES, both using machinery that already existed and was default-off.

1. PER-CELL SEEDING. `CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_SEED` composes `base*1000 + attempt`.
   Set per (arm, trial):
     - base VARIES WITH TRIAL, because attempt is the RETRY index. One fixed base
       for a whole arm would give trials 0/1/2 identical seeds and collapse three
       replicates into one measurement repeated three times -- destroying the very
       thing TRIALS exists for.
     - base is IDENTICAL ACROSS THE COMPARED ARMS, which makes this a PAIRED
       comparison. Both models meet the same sampling randomness on the same cell,
       so the dominant noise is DIFFERENCED OUT rather than averaged over. That is
       strictly stronger than anything 3 unpinned trials could give.
   Default-off is correct for the SCORED agent -- changing how it samples would be
   a behaviour change, not a measurement change. This is a measurement.

2. AN A/A CONTROL ARM. gemma against itself at a different seed base, so the gap
   it produces IS the noise floor for this configuration. Gemma rather than Qwen
   because it is ~6 min/cell against ~72, so the floor costs ~4h instead of ~16.
   `qwen38_27b_aa` is defined and can be run if the A/B gap lands close enough that
   a per-model floor matters.

Sequence is now qwen38_27b -> gemma31b -> gemma31b_aa.

This is the seventh borrowed constant examined in this harness and the second one
worth keeping (after TRIALS): the seed default is right for the shipped agent and
wrong for a measurement, which is a distinction the docstring makes explicitly and
I had not read until asked why 3 trials.
